                        "sense_id": "2d4e7d4d-6d6d-3249-b305-59903a35b00b",
                        "entry_id": "41c31790-df4f-3ea4-a4d0-91558b743c25",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The section of a primary school for the education of younger children, typically the classes of reception or kindergarten and years (grades) one and two."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "97be3eec-f78b-49a5-8cec-e73d8c43ba58",
                                "sense_id": "2d4e7d4d-6d6d-3249-b305-59903a35b00b",
                                "text": "Near-synonym: infant school"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d59a8c7a-7be1-4e50-9c85-5edcac82b092",
                                "sense_id": "2d4e7d4d-6d6d-3249-b305-59903a35b00b",
                                "text": "It was around the time I moved from infants to juniors, which was based in a different building, so it felt like going to big school."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb419710-c60c-4704-9d1f-2d6b6e65145b",
                                "sense_id": "2d4e7d4d-6d6d-3249-b305-59903a35b00b",
                                "text": "Although of course we did harder work in the juniors than we did in infants, there were still times when we relaxed and just enjoyed ourselves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78539c3d-01f8-4d1b-9fac-56f0dba84cb2",
                                "sense_id": "2d4e7d4d-6d6d-3249-b305-59903a35b00b",
                                "text": "George had Josh's form tutor for science, and she talked down to them, like they were still in infants, whereas Mr. Barton treated them like adults."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
